spec: S26-01, S26-02, S26-03

`vault list | create | rename | delete` (CMD-5) on the shared store, in a group of its own: it
adds Vaults while it runs (a `push` without `--vault` in a parallel case would see two and stop)
and deletes them again before the next group. `vault rename` points the local profile whose
Vault it was at the new name; `vault delete` clears it. Every exit path: 1 (empty name), 2
(unknown — naming the new name once a Vault was renamed away), 4 (owner-only), 5 (taken, still
holds a Document). Merged stdout+stderr; ages are `[..]`.

```console
$ annotary -p rowan vault create e2e-drafts
e2e-drafts	0	0	[..]

$ annotary -p rowan vault create e2e-drafts
? 5
error: Vault e2e-drafts already exists

$ annotary -p agent vault create e2e-mine
? 4
error: vault create is owner-only — ask an owner (`annotary member list` shows who)

$ annotary -p rowan vault create " "
? 1
error: NAME must not be empty — `annotary vault list` shows the Vaults

$ sh add-profile.sh
profile "e2e" saved → [..]/config.toml

$ annotary -p rowan vault rename e2e-drafts e2e-reviews
profile "e2e" now uses Vault "e2e-reviews"
e2e-reviews	0	0	[..]

$ annotary -p rowan profile list --json name,vault
[{"name":"agent","vault":"notes"},{"name":"down"},{"name":"e2e","vault":"e2e-reviews"},{"name":"limited"},{"name":"pw"},{"name":"rowan"}]

$ annotary -p rowan vault rename e2e-drafts e2e-x
? 2
error: no Vault e2e-drafts — Vault e2e-drafts was renamed to e2e-reviews

$ annotary -p rowan vault rename e2e-reviews notes
? 5
error: Vault notes already exists

$ annotary -p agent vault rename e2e-reviews e2e-x
? 4
error: vault rename is owner-only — ask an owner (`annotary member list` shows who)

$ annotary -p agent vault list
notes	[..]
e2e-reviews	0	0	[..]

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p rowan vault list
NAME         DOCUMENTS  DELETED  CREATED
notes        [..]
e2e-reviews  0          0        [..]

$ annotary -p rowan vault list --json name
[{"name":"notes"},{"name":"e2e-reviews"}]

$ annotary -p rowan push vdoc.md --vault e2e-reviews
vdoc	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan vault delete e2e-reviews
? 5
error: Vault e2e-reviews still holds 1 Document — delete and purge its Documents first (`annotary purge DOC`), then delete the Vault

$ annotary -p rowan delete vdoc.md
vdoc	[..]	deleted

$ annotary -p rowan vault delete e2e-reviews
? 5
error: Vault e2e-reviews still holds 1 Document (1 deleted — purge them first) — delete and purge its Documents first (`annotary purge DOC`), then delete the Vault

$ annotary -p rowan purge vdoc.md
purged vdoc ([..]) — 2 blobs removed
vdoc	[..]	purged

$ annotary -p agent vault delete e2e-reviews
? 4
error: vault delete is owner-only — ask an owner (`annotary member list` shows who)

$ annotary -p rowan vault delete e2e-reviews
profile "e2e" no longer names a Vault ("e2e-reviews" was deleted)
e2e-reviews	deleted

$ annotary -p rowan vault delete e2e-reviews
? 2
error: no Vault e2e-reviews — `GET /api/v1/vaults` lists them

$ annotary -p rowan vault create e2e-json --json
{"name":"e2e-json","documents":0,"deleted":0,"created":"[..]","id":"[..]"}

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p rowan vault delete e2e-json
e2e-json  deleted

$ annotary -p rowan -q profile remove e2e
profile "e2e" removed → [..]/config.toml

$ annotary -p rowan vault list --json name
[{"name":"notes"}]

```
